      "reasoning": "The learner has correctly identified that a catalyst increases rate but is using the common misconception that faster product formation means a greater equilibrium yield. Use an everyday analogy and ask one focused question about whether a catalyst changes the balance or only the speed of moving in both directions.",
      "content": "Think of two rooms connected by a doorway, with people moving in both directions. A catalyst is a bit like making that doorway easier to pass through: movement can happen faster, but that alone does not decide how many people will be in each room once things settle.\n\nFor this reversible reaction, does a catalyst speed up only the forward reaction, or both the forward and reverse reactions?"
    },
