    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "reasoning": "The learner needs a calm starting point and has not yet identified the option. Give the key distinction briefly: only temperature changes Kc. Then ask one focused question about the direction favoured by lowering temperature for an exothermic forward reaction, without naming the answer.",
      "content": "Take it one step at a time. A change in pressure can shift the equilibrium position, but it does not change the value of \\(K_c\\) when the temperature stays the same. Here, the forward reaction is exothermic, so which temperature change favours the forward reaction: an increase or a decrease?"
